Assertions:
[STATUS] the AUTH call and every POST/GET above return 200 {OBSERVED}
[BODY] RUN1 notification: finished = true, description = "Indexation completed successfully", errorCount = 0, totalCount > 0 and processedCount = totalCount {OBSERVED}
[BODY] RUN2 notification (the run that needs the lock RUN1 just held): finished = true, description = "Indexation completed successfully", errorCount = 0, totalCount > 0 {OBSERVED}
[BODY] RUN2 errors[] does not contain "Indexation is already in progress." {OBSERVED}
[BODY] C1 > 0 and C1 = C0 (an unchanged catalog is re-indexed in full; if the catalog was edited meanwhile the difference must equal the edits, otherwise BLOCKED as drift) {SPEC}

[STATUS] every call returns 200 and the GraphQL responses carry no errors[] {OBSERVED}
[BODY] RUN notification: finished = true, description = "Indexation completed successfully", errorCount = 0, totalCount > 0 {OBSERVED}
[BODY] C1 > 0 and C1 = C0 (full index after the swap); D1 is later than D0 {SPEC}
[DATA] every X_during sample > 0 and X1 = X0 (storefront category search never goes empty, and is complete after the swap) {SPEC}

[STATUS] every call returns 200 {OBSERVED}
[BODY] DOC notification: finished = true, description = "Indexation completed successfully", errorCount = 0, documentType = "Product" {OBSERVED}
[BODY] the document is present before and after and D1 is later than D0 (the per-product build really wrote the document) {SPEC}
[BODY] DOC errors[] does not contain "Indexation is already in progress." {OBSERVED}

[STATUS] every call returns 200 {OBSERVED}
[BODY] B_EARLY: finished = true, errorCount >= 1, errors[] contains "Indexation is already in progress." {OBSERVED}
[BODY] B_EARLY description is not "Indexation completed successfully" {OBSERVED}
[BODY] A_FINAL: finished = true, description = "Indexation completed successfully", errorCount = 0, totalCount > 0 and processedCount = totalCount (the winner is not disturbed) {OBSERVED}
[BODY] C1 > 0 and C1 = C0 {SPEC}

[STATUS] every call returns 200 {OBSERVED}
[BODY] DOC notification (read before A finished): finished = true, errorCount >= 1, errors[] contains "Indexation is already in progress.", description is not "Indexation completed successfully" {OBSERVED}
[BODY] CTRL notification (lock free): finished = true, description = "Indexation completed successfully", errorCount = 0 {OBSERVED}
[BODY] D1 is later than D0 (the product document is written by the control run that held the lock) {SPEC}

[STATUS] the cancel call returns 200 and every other call returns 200 {OBSERVED}
[BODY] A_FINAL: finished = true and description = "Indexation has been canceled" (cancellation reached the work that runs under the lock token) {OBSERVED}
[BODY] NEXT notification: finished = true, description = "Indexation completed successfully", errorCount = 0, totalCount > 0 - the lock was released by the cancelled run {OBSERVED}
[BODY] NEXT errors[] does not contain "Indexation is already in progress." {OBSERVED}
[BODY] C1 > 0 {SPEC}
